WEBVTT

00:12.970 --> 00:18.710
Hikari ga sasu sora, umareochiru kage
In the bright sky illuminated by
sunlight, darkened shadows are born.

00:18.810 --> 00:24.150
Unmei wa dokomademo hikisakareru
Fate itself is being torn apart.

00:25.190 --> 00:30.150
Donna toki mo kesshite akiramenainara
If you never give up, no matter what happens,

00:30.330 --> 00:37.560
mada tozasareteru tobira kanarazu hiraku
Even that locked door will open for you.

00:38.530 --> 00:43.990
Eien datte dakishimete, fuuin mo tokihanachi
Embrace eternity and release the seal.

00:44.070 --> 00:49.940
Mamorubekimono ga ima kokoni wa arukara
Because the ones you wish
to protect are right here.

00:49.940 --> 00:55.880
Namida mo gyutto dakishimete,
yasashisa de tsutsumikomi
Embrace their tears with kindness.

00:55.880 --> 01:01.560
Nagareru mizu no youni tsuyoku nare
Become strong like the formless water,

01:01.560 --> 01:07.550
omouyouni tsuyoku nare
Become as strong as you wish to be.

01:07.700 --> 01:13.170
Mou jibun ni obienaide
Stop being afraid of yourself.

01:13.170 --> 01:19.800
Sou mirai wo osorenaide
Do not fear the future.

01:42.830 --> 01:44.590
Did you wet the bed again?

01:48.740 --> 01:50.970
Go take a shower to clean yourself up...

01:51.810 --> 01:54.670
Just put your clothes in the washing machine...

01:54.940 --> 01:57.350
After you wash up, you can sleep in my bed.

01:57.350 --> 01:58.570
What about you?

01:59.110 --> 02:01.380
I need to go clean your sheets.

02:09.760 --> 02:15.320
I probably only had that dream because
I saw Toru taking care of Shiro-chan...

02:17.230 --> 02:22.330
I guess he's all grown up now.
He's even taking care of someone else.

02:24.840 --> 02:27.360
Come to think of it,
I was just a kid back then, too.

02:27.840 --> 02:30.240
How did I manage to take care of him like that?

02:31.210 --> 02:33.150
Oh yeah...

02:34.820 --> 02:37.080
I only cared for him like how I was cared for.

02:39.020 --> 02:42.620
The sun came up as I thought about that.

02:43.890 --> 02:48.830
Our Fox Deity, Goes to Church

02:55.870 --> 02:58.710
Good morning, head of Mizuchi.

02:58.710 --> 03:00.070
Are you awake?

03:00.070 --> 03:01.340
I'm awake.

03:01.780 --> 03:03.750
Do you want breakfast?

03:03.750 --> 03:05.510
Of course I do!

03:05.580 --> 03:07.340
I-I'm sorry!

03:10.120 --> 03:11.750
Geez...

03:24.470 --> 03:27.400
Food gets kind of plain here
when Noboru isn't around.

03:37.280 --> 03:38.140
Mamorime.

03:38.880 --> 03:39.610
Yes?

03:39.910 --> 03:42.350
Stop throwing salt at the laundry.

03:44.690 --> 03:45.480
But...

03:45.850 --> 03:48.120
Noboru had this troubled look on his face.

03:48.120 --> 03:49.050
Then I shall stop.

03:50.890 --> 03:52.460
I'm going out for a walk.

03:52.460 --> 03:54.090
Watch Toru for me.

04:05.210 --> 04:06.500
Ebisu isn't here?

04:06.670 --> 04:08.310
He has gone to Izumo.

04:08.310 --> 04:11.340
Oh, right. It's October...

04:11.610 --> 04:16.380
Yes. All the gods of Japan gather
at Izumo during this month.

04:16.520 --> 04:17.750
Is something the matter?

04:18.390 --> 04:21.150
The head of the Mizuchi was kidnapped?!

04:21.690 --> 04:24.090
I'm going to make a deal with the kidnappers...

04:24.830 --> 04:29.100
I already asked the Mamorime,
but I want you two to look after Toru as well.

04:29.100 --> 04:30.330
Understood.

04:30.500 --> 04:34.800
Protecting the safety of this
land's parishioners is our duty.

04:34.800 --> 04:38.170
We still owe the head of the
Mizuchi for that fried rice.

04:38.170 --> 04:39.260
I'm counting on you.

04:46.450 --> 04:49.310
San Steroa Church Sale

05:01.300 --> 05:02.500
Look!

05:02.500 --> 05:03.520
He looks so cute...

05:11.540 --> 05:13.840
I can't... Not now...

05:22.220 --> 05:24.180
That's odd...

05:24.550 --> 05:26.320
The needle is pointing at him?

05:26.590 --> 05:28.520
Yes, but Boss said...

05:28.760 --> 05:29.810
I am Kugen.

05:30.930 --> 05:35.190
You are the tenko Kugen?
I heard you always take the form of a woman...

05:35.460 --> 05:37.660
Well, whatever...

05:37.930 --> 05:42.270
To prevent your using of the kotodama,
we will introduce ourselves before you ask.

05:42.270 --> 05:44.070
I am Naguma.

05:44.340 --> 05:45.570
I am Shimenogi.

05:46.310 --> 05:47.100
Where is Noboru?

05:47.240 --> 05:48.370
You have to bring out the Byakki first!

05:48.780 --> 05:51.640
Byakki? What's that?

05:53.650 --> 05:54.410
It's over here...

05:59.190 --> 06:00.820
Here we go...

06:00.820 --> 06:03.020
Did you really put her in here?

06:03.020 --> 06:03.720
Yeah.

06:07.800 --> 06:09.730
The baku is coming!

06:09.730 --> 06:15.800
The baku is coming! The baku is coming!
The baku is coming!

06:21.640 --> 06:22.510
They're!

06:24.010 --> 06:24.770
Oni?!

06:25.550 --> 06:28.740
The oni have been up to something recently.

06:34.020 --> 06:35.510
I've brought your food.

06:43.330 --> 06:44.230
Sir?

06:46.100 --> 06:47.570
Sir! What are you?!

06:54.680 --> 06:56.700
What is this?!

07:01.280 --> 07:03.320
I can't pick up Noboru's scent...

07:03.320 --> 07:09.810
The father of the current head should have
received a message on his cell phone earlier.

07:10.460 --> 07:11.890
Phones...

07:12.660 --> 07:14.990
I can just tell them no one
came to receive the package...

07:24.610 --> 07:27.010
Excuse me. Can I use your phone?

07:27.940 --> 07:30.540
Sure. Go right ahead.

07:33.580 --> 07:34.880
Let's see...

07:35.020 --> 07:37.420
Uhh, it's 090...

07:37.520 --> 07:43.890
OSTRICH-MAN...

07:52.330 --> 07:57.500
That's odd. I thought I
dialed Noboru's cell phone...

08:02.210 --> 08:05.740
I was so careless! I didn't know the
Kugen fox could turn into a man!

08:05.850 --> 08:07.580
She was a woman just yesterday!

08:12.220 --> 08:14.280
You're not getting away from me...

08:43.220 --> 08:44.880
You scared me...

08:48.960 --> 08:51.520
Say, Shiro-chan. Where did you come from?

08:53.330 --> 08:54.450
You don't know?

08:55.560 --> 08:56.690
What about your family?

08:59.400 --> 09:00.420
You don't have one?

09:01.600 --> 09:02.900
You don't know?

09:05.470 --> 09:06.910
That sounds sad.

09:09.180 --> 09:10.730
Don't you feel lonely?

09:11.250 --> 09:13.580
Do you understand what lonely means?

09:15.480 --> 09:17.470
Have you ever felt lonely?

09:17.850 --> 09:19.510
Shiro-chan!

09:19.690 --> 09:22.660
There we go. Are you okay?

09:26.990 --> 09:30.120
What to do now...

09:31.170 --> 09:34.260
I know. Why don't you join our family?

09:37.370 --> 09:40.140
That sounds like I want to marry her...

09:42.180 --> 09:44.080
Just kidding.

09:45.850 --> 09:47.940
Toru-san seems to be safe.

09:48.220 --> 09:51.150
But is that his girlfriend next to him?

09:51.650 --> 09:54.710
To think he would choose a girl
wrapped up in enchanted cloth...

09:55.460 --> 09:58.150
I knew he would have extraordinary tastes.

10:00.360 --> 10:07.320
I expected to find some clues by following
the servants of the presiding deity...

10:07.740 --> 10:08.570
And I was right.

10:42.770 --> 10:43.530
Crap!

10:49.710 --> 10:53.770
By the way, it would be in your best
interests to refrain from using spells.

10:53.950 --> 10:58.850
The Mirror Reflect spell has been cast
on the doors and walls of this room.

10:59.190 --> 11:03.090
Attack anything here and it
will all bounce back at you.

11:03.290 --> 11:06.890
Just stay there for the time being...

11:07.430 --> 11:08.760
Dammit!

11:10.600 --> 11:13.160
He got away?!

11:13.530 --> 11:16.940
Shimenogi and Naguma haven't returned
since they went out for the exchange...

11:17.100 --> 11:20.230
The others are currently
searching for the Mizuchi head.

11:20.370 --> 11:21.930
I'm so sorry!

11:22.180 --> 11:25.870
There's no need to worry. This entire
building functions as a type of barrier.

11:26.150 --> 11:29.980
Being an ordinary human, the Mizuchi head
will not be able to escape of his own accord...

11:30.120 --> 11:30.990
Because...

11:30.990 --> 11:35.960
...of this spell I purchased off
the internet black market!

11:35.960 --> 11:38.930
It can completely hinder a
human's sense of direction!

11:39.130 --> 11:41.420
It's called the Human Roach Motel!

11:41.660 --> 11:45.030
Didn't you buy the Mirror
Reflect spell online, too?

11:45.230 --> 11:49.070
Anyway, the Mizuchi head must
be somewhere in the building!

11:49.340 --> 11:50.300
Find him!

11:50.400 --> 11:50.960
Yes, ma'am!

12:05.850 --> 12:07.590
Where's the exit?!

12:07.590 --> 12:09.820
This house is way too big!

12:27.680 --> 12:28.840
Hello?!

12:30.180 --> 12:31.870
Hey. Is that you, Mubyo?

12:32.150 --> 12:35.640
Are you the big brother? Wait, who are you?

12:36.080 --> 12:39.050
This is Kugen. I'm calling from Noboru's cell.

12:39.050 --> 12:41.150
Isn't your voice a bit too deep?

12:41.390 --> 12:43.220
I'm a man right now.

12:43.520 --> 12:45.650
Oh, okay. So what do you want?

12:45.930 --> 12:47.260
There's a door in front of me...

12:47.430 --> 12:50.900
I want to get past it, but it's locked.

12:50.900 --> 12:53.700
Then use a spell and break it.
You're good at that, aren't you?

12:53.700 --> 12:55.730
The Mirror Reflect spell is on it.

12:55.970 --> 12:57.160
Oh.

12:57.470 --> 13:00.130
That's why I need you to use your kotodama.

13:01.480 --> 13:03.100
I'm in Akagi right now...

13:03.610 --> 13:05.640
I know you are, too.

13:05.980 --> 13:09.940
You may be a god, but you're only a substitute.
There's no reason for you to go to Izumo.

13:10.150 --> 13:11.520
Well, excuse me!

13:11.850 --> 13:16.720
Being the presiding god here, you should be
able to unlock a door with just your kotodama.

13:17.320 --> 13:18.690
Across the phone?

13:18.860 --> 13:21.500
The only thing you need to use the kotodama is...

13:21.500 --> 13:27.800
The voice of the caster, target, and a
means to transmit your voice to the target.

13:29.300 --> 13:30.330
I'll give it a try.

13:30.500 --> 13:31.970
Face the phone to the door.

13:37.280 --> 13:38.110
Open.

13:40.010 --> 13:42.020
It opened! Thanks!

13:42.020 --> 13:44.280
H-Hey, wait! What's going on?!

13:45.190 --> 13:46.920
This can be pretty convenient.

13:50.860 --> 13:53.190
This is a church...

13:55.160 --> 13:57.600
You can't escape, head of Mizuchi.

14:07.410 --> 14:09.840
Now let us go.

14:21.160 --> 14:22.950
Hey, there you are.

14:23.090 --> 14:23.890
Ku!

14:25.060 --> 14:29.700
I suppose you're also an oni, sister...

14:29.700 --> 14:31.670
An oni? Her?!

14:32.570 --> 14:38.030
Yeah, an oni. Drifters with neither
their own land nor spiritual powers...

14:38.210 --> 14:41.770
We may not have spiritual powers,
but we have the power of the internet!

14:43.280 --> 14:49.880
Noboru, you're the last person
I thought would get kidnapped.

14:50.120 --> 14:55.110
Let me guess. Some girl lured you out.

14:56.090 --> 14:58.560
Your breaking through that door is impressive.

14:59.830 --> 15:00.850
However!

15:09.600 --> 15:11.300
Get him!

15:12.010 --> 15:12.730
Ku!

15:12.970 --> 15:13.600
Wait!

15:41.540 --> 15:43.370
A monster of fire...

15:43.600 --> 15:47.560
I need water... No, just something
to extinguish the flames!

16:05.630 --> 16:08.650
Sand can put out fire...

16:11.870 --> 16:13.770
Why are you doing this?!

16:13.770 --> 16:16.700
Because Kugen stole the Byakki from us!

16:16.700 --> 16:17.710
Byakki?

16:17.710 --> 16:20.570
She should have been delivered
to you sometime this week!

16:24.850 --> 16:27.440
She belongs to our clan...

16:28.050 --> 16:33.580
The oni were called the defiant ones for
hundreds of years before I was even born.

16:34.020 --> 16:37.550
That was the reasoning the
gods used to take her from us...

16:37.790 --> 16:40.450
And we've finally come so
close to getting her back...

16:41.230 --> 16:42.730
No! It's just a misunderstanding!

16:42.730 --> 16:46.530
The packing slip said it was made out
to Takagami Toru!

16:46.630 --> 16:48.360
It's another trick played by that fox.

16:48.540 --> 16:49.940
Ku would never do anything like that!

16:49.940 --> 16:51.670
As the head of the Mizuchi family...

16:51.670 --> 16:55.340
...you should know why that fox
was sealed in the first place.

16:55.980 --> 16:56.910
But...

16:57.240 --> 16:59.410
You just don't know of its true nature...

17:00.180 --> 17:03.670
What about you?! What do you know about Ku?!

17:08.090 --> 17:09.580
What is it?

17:12.730 --> 17:13.750
Ku!

17:15.360 --> 17:16.760
I-Impossible!

17:16.900 --> 17:21.160
I messed with that car before
going inside the building.

17:22.070 --> 17:25.730
You were just tricked into
going around in circles.

17:27.610 --> 17:30.700
You will now return what
you have taken from us!

17:30.840 --> 17:33.250
I keep telling you I don't
know anything about it...

17:33.250 --> 17:35.680
You're still playing dumb with me?!
It's the Byakki!

17:35.680 --> 17:37.810
Return the Byakki to us at once!

17:38.150 --> 17:43.120
I keep telling you! I don't even
know what this Byakki is!

17:43.120 --> 17:44.090
It's Shiro-chan.

17:45.190 --> 17:47.390
Shiro-chan is the Byakki.

17:49.230 --> 17:51.860
The Byakki is the one and only white oni.

17:52.370 --> 17:53.990
She is an oni with no horns.

17:54.700 --> 17:59.930
Until her awakening, she does
nothing and says nothing.

18:00.510 --> 18:02.480
She appears dead, yet she is not.

18:03.210 --> 18:05.200
She appears alive, yet she is not.

18:05.850 --> 18:08.010
Her existence is special.

18:08.820 --> 18:12.620
And her existence brings legitimacy to
one's rightful place as the lord of the oni.

18:12.620 --> 18:16.280
The lord of the oni? Is that what you want to be?

18:16.690 --> 18:21.150
As you have said, we are drifters
with no land we can call home...

18:21.800 --> 18:25.890
We steal for our day-to-day livelihood.

18:26.530 --> 18:31.900
You may not understand us,
but that is why we need a lord.

18:32.540 --> 18:37.640
One who can organize us.
One who can return our dignity to us!

18:38.250 --> 18:42.610
So please return the Byakki to us...

18:43.680 --> 18:44.510
Please...

18:48.290 --> 18:49.810
Very well. I'll return her to you.

18:50.420 --> 18:51.190
Ku!

18:51.460 --> 18:54.120
She belonged to them in the first place.

18:54.500 --> 18:56.630
If she belongs to them,
then we have to return her.

18:56.630 --> 18:57.320
But!

18:57.900 --> 19:01.860
I doubt you intended to look after her forever.

19:02.070 --> 19:04.900
Y-Yeah, but...

19:09.280 --> 19:12.800
So this is the pitcher. And that's the catcher!

19:13.350 --> 19:14.210
Do you understand?

19:18.320 --> 19:19.620
Hey! Noboru!

19:22.290 --> 19:23.310
You are...

19:30.260 --> 19:32.030
So you were Takagami Toru?

19:32.200 --> 19:35.600
Enju-san, right? What are you doing here?

19:45.210 --> 19:48.620
We have come for you, Byakki-sama...

19:48.620 --> 19:49.710
Come for her?

19:53.690 --> 19:55.180
Shiro-chan...

20:01.500 --> 20:05.760
We will leave this land.
I doubt we will ever meet again.

20:09.370 --> 20:12.700
Please excuse our prior actions against you.

20:13.510 --> 20:16.240
But also understand our will...

20:16.980 --> 20:20.310
Our last struggle to live using
what little pride we have left...

20:20.610 --> 20:23.340
Even if you don't survive, I think
some things would never vanish.

20:24.420 --> 20:27.110
But I wouldn't know anything about it...

20:27.390 --> 20:31.150
Shiro-chan, you're going home, right?

20:34.430 --> 20:37.300
I guess you would be happier with your family...

20:38.630 --> 20:40.360
This is for the best...

20:44.340 --> 20:46.330
This is for the best, right?

20:57.380 --> 20:58.150
Ko!

21:04.260 --> 21:06.690
Are you sure about this, Chief?

21:06.690 --> 21:10.320
We found the Byakki, but we're letting it go?

21:10.630 --> 21:14.360
Those oni have no way of releasing
the powers of the Byakki.

21:15.370 --> 21:19.360
The eyes of the Byakki were open,
meaning the imprinting is already complete.

21:19.810 --> 21:22.780
Besides, those oni simply purchased it...

21:23.010 --> 21:26.880
Don't forget about the thief who stole it
from us and sent it to Takagami Toru...

21:27.910 --> 21:30.180
We have to find out who that is...

21:40.290 --> 21:46.760
sora no hate ga tsunagaru basho wo
Where the horizon meets the earth,

21:47.230 --> 21:54.470
no ni saku hana wa mada kitto shiranai
The flower growing in the wild remains unaware.

21:55.810 --> 22:02.310
Kokoyori ii sekai ga aruto
While thinking that there
is a world better than this.

22:02.480 --> 22:10.080
Kokoro wa itsumo hane wo hirogetagaru
They always desire to spread
the wings of their hearts.

22:11.020 --> 22:18.020
Yume dakede owarasenai
Don't let it end as just a dream,

22:18.630 --> 22:25.130
chansu ga aru hazusa
There's always a chance.

22:25.370 --> 22:32.780
Daijoubu bokura ha hitori janai
It's all right. We are not alone.

22:32.780 --> 22:40.420
Kaze ga nanika wo iouto shiteru
The winds are telling us something.

22:40.420 --> 22:48.060
Daijoubu kanarazu umaku yareru
It's all right. You can do it.

22:48.060 --> 22:59.300
Omoi wa itsuka jibun wo kaeru michi ni naru
Those dreams are a path you'll change yourself.

23:06.910 --> 23:09.880
Toru. Toru.

23:11.320 --> 23:12.510
Toru.

23:21.800 --> 23:22.990
Shiro-chan...

23:24.900 --> 23:25.730
Next Time

23:25.730 --> 23:27.730
Next Time
Shiro-chan awakened as the Byakki.

23:27.730 --> 23:27.870
Next Time

23:27.870 --> 23:30.900
Next Time
Now the war over controlling the Byakki begins.

23:30.900 --> 23:31.070
Next Time

23:31.070 --> 23:34.040
Next Time
I'm powerless, so what can I do to stop it?

23:34.040 --> 23:34.570
Next Time

23:34.570 --> 23:35.040
Next Time
Next time, "Our Fox Deity, Perseveres."

23:35.040 --> 23:36.810
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Perseveres
Next time, "Our Fox Deity, Perseveres."

23:36.810 --> 23:37.040
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Perseveres

23:37.040 --> 23:39.180
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Perseveres
You're only a man when you're depended on.

23:39.180 --> 23:39.840
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Perseveres
